WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.620
Imagine a world where everyone is
free, and no one ever chooses evil.

2
00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.410
In 1955, J.

3
00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:07.560
L.

4
00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:13.390
Mackie and Antony Flew argued that an
all-powerful God could have made that world.

5
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.610
Then, in 1974, Alvin Plantinga replied.

6
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.660
He offered a defence, not a theodicy.

7
00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:24.880
So could God make people who
are free but never choose evil?

8
00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.630
And if not, was freedom worth it?

9
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.670
In this mission, you'll follow the
free will defence step by step,

10
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.190
and its critics.

11
00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.290
Then you'll ask whether belief in one
God can be defended in the face of evil

12
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.450
at all.

13
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.650
Your mission: weigh up whether God could
make free people who never choose evil.
